# File Storage

This app ships with a storage manager backed by `github.com/goforj/storage`.

The generated setup uses:

- one default disk
- many named disks
- the same API regardless of backend

## Defaults

By default, the scaffold defines:

- the default disk from `STORAGE_*` -> `storage/app/private`
- a named `public` disk from `STORAGE_PUBLIC_*` -> `storage/app/public`

The generated app can also define additional named disks through `STORAGE_<NAME>_*` variables.

## Configuration

Use these environment variables:

```env
STORAGE_DRIVER=local
STORAGE_ROOT=storage/app/private
STORAGE_PREFIX=

STORAGE_PUBLIC_DRIVER=local
STORAGE_PUBLIC_ROOT=storage/app/public

STORAGE_AVATARS_DRIVER=s3
STORAGE_AVATARS_BUCKET=my-app-uploads
STORAGE_AVATARS_REGION=us-east-1
STORAGE_AVATARS_PREFIX=avatars
```

Supported drivers in the scaffold resolver:

- `local`
- `memory`
- `redis`
- `ftp`
- `sftp`
- `s3`
- `gcs`
- `dropbox`
- `rclone`

Common env vars:

| Env var suffix | Value type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| DRIVER | string | local |
| PREFIX | string | empty |

Driver-specific env vars:

| Driver | Env var suffix | Value type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| local | ROOT | path | storage/app/private for the default disk, storage/app/public for the public disk, or the local driver fallback |
| memory | none | n/a | no driver-specific env vars |
| redis | ADDR | host:port | REDIS_HOST:REDIS_PORT or redis:6379 |
| redis | USERNAME | string | empty |
| redis | PASSWORD | string | REDIS_PASSWORD or empty |
| redis | DB | integer | 0 |
| ftp | HOST | host | empty |
| ftp | PORT | integer | 21 |
| ftp | USER | string | empty |
| ftp | PASSWORD | string | empty |
| ftp | TLS | boolean | false |
| ftp | INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY | boolean | false |
| sftp | HOST | host | empty |
| sftp | PORT | integer | 22 |
| sftp | USER | string | root |
| sftp | PASSWORD | string | empty |
| sftp | KEY_PATH | path | empty |
| sftp | KNOWN_HOSTS_PATH | path | empty |
| sftp | INSECURE_IGNORE_HOST_KEY | boolean | false |
| s3 | BUCKET | string | empty |
| s3 | ENDPOINT | URL | empty |
| s3 | REGION | string | us-east-1 |
| s3 | ACCESS_KEY_ID | string | empty |
